    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d825">

                <pb facs="1056" n="954" xml:id="pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/120: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-09T20:00:00-05:00">January 9, 1935—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Your 14, January 7, 7 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d825-f1"/> as a basis for
                    your conversation with the Ministry regarding Moroccan situation, in order to
                    avoid possible ambiguity with respect to the expiration of the Franco-British
                    accord, it is suggested that you eliminate the second paragraph on page 4 of the
                    Department’s instruction 669, December 18,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d825-f2"/> and
                    substitute for (1) on same page the second sentence at top of page 2 of the note
                        enclosed<anchor n="14" xml:id="d825-f3"/> with the above instruction from
                    Ponsot to Laboulaye which refers to the expiration of the period of 30 years for
                    which the maintenance of the principle of commercial liberty was
                    contemplated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
